# scripts/audit-native.allow
#
# Packages permitted to have build dependencies on C/C++/asm compilers (cc, cmake,
# nasm-rs, bindgen, autotools) or ship C/C++/assembly source files.
#
# Format:
#   <crate-name>    <reason>
#
# Lines starting with '#' and blank lines are ignored.
# Each entry below was checked on 2026-10-29: the files ship in the crate's
# tarball, but nothing in Latch's build compiles them.
objc-sys                  headers for the GNUstep/ObjFW runtimes; build.rs only links Apple's system libobjc unless the unstable-exception feature (off) is on
ttf-parser                testing-tools/ (a Qt font viewer) in the tarball; no build.rs
webbrowser                an iOS test app's header in tests/; no build.rs
alsa-sys                  wrapper.h is for the optional use-bindgen feature (off); build.rs only asks pkg-config for the system libasound (Linux's sound API)
cc                        src/detect_compiler_family.c is cc's own probe file; cc is built only as wayland-backend's build dependency and is never run (see below)
nix                       a kernel-module test fixture in test/; no build.rs
wayland-backend           log_shim.c is compiled only with the log feature (off); without it build.rs compiles nothing
wayland-protocols-plasma  an upstream autotest in plasma-wayland-protocols/; no build.rs
